{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game","id":391478,"title":"Have you ever adapted a PreExisting story for a Game? (","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-03T08:54:46-08:00","id":391478,"title":"Have you ever adapted a PreExisting story for a Game? (","content":"i been thinking about making one of my players more Constantine-esque. and i been tempted on adapting the story of Newcastle for one of my players..so, have you ever done something of the like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:15:41-08:00","id":391502,"title":"","content":"Did a hunters hunted/sorcerer game using Constantine concept as the base line. Was interesting, but fairly short. Humans are squishy in the WoD. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:47:26-08:00","id":391675,"title":"","content":"I ran a one shot Hunters Hunted game which was pretty much the movie Virus only replace the living electricity and borg monsters with vampires. I'm also going to be running a short Mage game at some point somewhat based off of part 4 of Jo Jo's Bizarre Adventure: Diamond is Unbreakable. I've also been playing around with the idea of running a Resident Evil Raccoon City Chronicle using Hunters Hunted at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:52:32-08:00","id":391678,"title":"","content":"A fair few times - consciously and unconsciously.<br /> <br /> The obvious thing to note is that a story generally has a set beginning, middle and end, and doesn't give you any ideas for what to do if the player does something different than the original protagonist, so it's a good idea to think about alternative outcomes in advance. In this example, is there a way to save Astra?<br /> <br /> The other risk is that the players know the story as well and recognise it. Changing names and locations can help, but only to a certain extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:49:19-08:00","id":391771,"title":"","content":"Have used other universes for inspiration and influence on my games and characters? Yes.<br /> <br /> Have I run stories through RPGs? At most, sort of but again its more akin to the above. When the Warhammer 40K RPG line, <i>Only War</i> came out I ran a game where they were a squad in the Valhallan 597th, the regiment of famed Commissar Ciaphas Cain. None of the players were playing Cain or the other notable members of the regiment but they interacted with several of them. While in terms of OWoD this past summer I played, and helped create, a Dark Ages: Werewolf game set in the world of A Song of Ice and Fire/Game of Thrones, albeit around ten years before Robert's Rebellion.<br /> <br /> Situations like that are about the closest I've come to playing or running actual stories from novels, films, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:13:01-08:00","id":391841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=391678#post391678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair few times - consciously and unconsciously.<br /> <br /> The obvious thing to note is that a story generally has a set beginning, middle and end, and doesn't give you any ideas for what to do if the player does something different than the original protagonist, so it's a good idea to think about alternative outcomes in advance. In this example, is there a way to save Astra?<br /> <br /> The other risk is that the players know the story as well and recognise it. Changing names and locations can help, but only to a certain extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>good thing my group only read manga xD<br /> <br /> Well, i like the idea of saving Astra..but at a price.<br /> <br /> <br /> also, funny enough whenever i run a game in the Trinity Continuum i usually do it during or soon after WW2 taking a LOT of elements out of Hellboy (Kroenen and The Black Flame).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:38:55-08:00","id":391868,"title":"","content":"I've run several games that loan bit's and pieces of several movies/books/comics/games but I don't think I've ever ran something close to as it happened in a singular source. Though closest would likely be my forthcoming, though I will ST a Rogue Trader game before this one, Umbrella special forces team game, that is actual Pentex 1st Team game, that will loan various bit's and pieces from Resident Evil franchise as a whole as well as L4D and other sources. But I'm fairly certain it will run somewhat of rails into the unknown soon after the players get through the chronicles starting chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T07:32:23-08:00","id":392577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=391771#post391771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in terms of OWoD this past summer I played, and helped create, a Dark Ages: Werewolf game set in the world of A Song of Ice and Fire/Game of Thrones, albeit around ten years before Robert's Rebellion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, tell us more. How did that work out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:19:54-08:00","id":392947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=392577#post392577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, tell us more. How did that work out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly well. We kept it just to DAW, though I did have some ideas with incorporating DAM as well but they weren't added. Also threw out and/or altered aspect of the Garou's history so it blended better with the ASoIF universe. Their origins have largely become lost and shrouded in myth. Gaia and the Triat may exist or simply a story that some Garou tell or something in between. The tension and division between the tribes was also much greater, partly because it fit the setting and partly because the BSD weren't really a thing. Individual BSD and packs of them do exist but there is no BSD tribe, just mad, corrupt and monstrous werewolves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:59:37-08:00","id":393154,"title":"","content":"One of my mage players got Fucked up, lost his Chantry. His companios are dead and his spaceship (he is playing in the umbra) got stolen by a Nephandi who was once his friend...oh and he lost an arm and an eye during the attack, PS. he is a Son of Ether..<br /> <br /> so i decided to do the honorable thing and allow him for him to be driven by mad vengeance, he knows someone betrayed him (other than his friend) and he decided to torture his crew so they learn not to mess with him.<br /> I added a new character, a lesser mage who is paraplegic, his name is Hewie, he is a 'Tecnocract Who Stands His Ground.' (he is not a technocratic union character but he belives in technocracy as a political system)<br /> <br /> <br /> So Yeah...i think my player is turning into the Big Boss","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T11:05:24-08:00","id":399034,"title":"","content":"In my Hunter: the Reckoning game, the PCs investigated a deadly fungus that was spreading through the Los Angeles sewers. They discovered it was tied into a series of blonde women being kidnapped, fungus-riddled mutants, and a massive mutated turtle who had sufficient intelligence to declare himself the king of the sewers. Further investigation determined that the &quot;mushroom men&quot; had a prophecy of a mustachioed hero in red who would defeat the sewer king, and so they had been kidnapping blonde women in hopes of luring the hero to help them.<br /> <br /> It took my players a surprisingly long time to figure out that the whole thing was (in-universe and out) an extended Super Mario Bros. reference. Once they got it, though, they figured out just where the hell this &quot;prophecy&quot; came from, and with great effort managed to... get all the mutants killed by the Technocracy. Yeah, they kind of screwed that one up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T09:28:17-08:00","id":404543,"title":"","content":"I built a whole Chronicle based on James Clavell's Tai-Pan adapting it over to a World of Darkness. I used Tai Pan as part of the backdrop to Hong Kong, while using WoD Hong Kong as a backdrop as well. Historically it was set just before the 2nd Opium War and ended in the aftermath of the 3rd Opium War.<br /> <br /> It was about the Western Supernaturals (Kindred, Garou, Changing Breeds) and the Eastern Supernaturals (KoTE and Hengoyakai) it turned out to be pretty interesting. Had nearly 50 playable things for players to play. I did not want to add in Mage, I felt I had enough for people and I had no idea on any good Mage SL and I did not want to work on how Mages worked at that time, I had enough to build as it was.Both Victorian Age Vampire and Werewolf Wyld West both helped out a lot but still had a lot to build. <br /> <br /> I spent a year making it ran for over a year. A lot of intrigue and such. It focused mostly on the Western characters because I only had one player ended up playing something from the East. It was great. <br /> <br /> When my computer crashed I lost all of it. Everything I made. It was a fun game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T09:42:28-08:00","id":404550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=392947#post392947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fairly well. We kept it just to DAW, though I did have some ideas with incorporating DAM as well but they weren't added. Also threw out and/or altered aspect of the Garou's history so it blended better with the ASoIF universe. Their origins have largely become lost and shrouded in myth. Gaia and the Triat may exist or simply a story that some Garou tell or something in between. The tension and division between the tribes was also much greater, partly because it fit the setting and partly because the BSD weren't really a thing. Individual BSD and packs of them do exist but there is no BSD tribe, just mad, corrupt and monstrous werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did White Walkers exist? Dragons? Did magic come back into the world as the story progressed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T17:44:55-08:00","id":405348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=404550#post404550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did White Walkers exist? Dragons? Did magic come back into the world as the story progressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said it was ten years before Robert's Rebellion so neither White Walkers, Dragons or magic (beyond the Rites and Gifts of the Garou and Spirits) featured in our game. But they did exist.<br /> <br /> The short version of the backstory was that several of the Tribes lived openly among the First Men as they came to Westeros. These tribes were the White Howlers, the Fianna, the Children of Gaia, the Red Talons and the Black Furies. They fought alongside their human kin against the Children of the Forest and further claim that it was one of their own, a CoG, that brokered the peace between them and came to serve as the keepers of that peace, ensuring that both sides honored the peace. When the Long Night and the White Walkers came, they were on the frontlines. Unfortunately their dead made for some of the most terrible wights around.<br /> <br /> However once the Long Night ended and the Wall was being built things began to fall apart among the tribes, with the Wall cutting the lands belonging to the White Howlers in half. Needless to say they weren't happy about this, fighting happened and the Howlers and their Wildling kin were pushed beyond the Wall and in the present the Howlers are seen as feral monsters that want nothing more to burn everything south of the Wall. Basically they see them as a non-corrupt, non-corrupting BSD.<br /> <br /> As I said, at that time the Garou lived openly with the First Men, with many of their noble families breeding with Garou, seeing it as a great honor to produce a Garou child. Indeed there were even Garou Kings from time to time that ruled both races.<br /> <br /> Then the Andals and those tribes that lived among them came. The Andal Tribes, the Silver Fangs, the Shadow Lords, the Gets of Fenris, the Bone Gnawers, the Warders of Man and the Silent Striders lived much as canon Garou with the Veil between them and humans. They also brought silver weapons, something the tribes of the First Men never encountered before and proved to be quite effective against them. In the end, even though the North never fell to the Andals they were forced to adopt the Veil as well, though much looser than in other parts of Westeros with several Stark Kings that were also Garou long after the Andal Invasion and even in the present every major Northern House still carries the blood of Garou. In fact the pack briefly met Roose Bolton, the new Lord of the Dreadfort and a Shadow Lord after he and his pack saved them.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the moment he revealed himself as Roose Bolton the rest of the table freaked out.<br /> <br /> There is only one place in all of Westeros that Garou have no presence, the Iron Islands. Ever since they first came to Westeros they felt a powerful but dormant, sinister presence beneath the islands, something that unnerves them. They believe it to be what the Ironborn revere as the Drown God and that first BSD came into existence because they went there. And when the Ironborn invaded the Riverlands they came with the largest number of BSD ever seen.<br /> <br /> When Aegon invaded the Garou at first did nothing, seeing it as merely another dispute between human kings and were much more busy with the BSD the Ironborn brought with them. It wasn't until Aegon torched Harrenhal that they realized just how dangerous he and his dragons were but before they could mount any proper kind of attack or defense, the Field of Fire happened and afterwards they decided to continue as they had so long as House Targaryen did not pose a treat to them. Though they had always been a little leery of the Targaryens and their dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T12:06:06-08:00","id":405988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=391841#post391841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">good thing my group only read manga xD</div> </div> </div> </div>the other way around, my group read only comics and Game of Thrones, so I usually adapt situations taken from manga and anime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T23:15:16-08:00","id":406386,"title":"","content":"We started in New York City: the whole city had been walled off into a giant prison. Our group of various WoD-type individuals were going to have to make our way through the gangs and politics of this un-managed prison-city... until our Mage used Correspondence to teleport out. He brought back guns and items, and we were able to break our way out.<br /> <br /> ... That's when we learned that giant ships were appearing in the sky over seemingly unimportant areas, which turned out to be Void Engineer ships that were sucking the Tass/Gnosis/Glamour out of areas in beams that then caused the areas to explode.<br /> <br /> We then managed to make our way up onto one of these ships and fought in a space battle... and that's when things got weird? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, we started with <b>'Escape from New York</b>&quot; and continued with &quot;<b>Independence Day</b>&quot; (because it had just come out) and moved into Anime things.<br /> <br /> We've also played in the setting of The Highlander as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:51:36-08:00","id":410135,"title":"","content":"At Christmas last year, I ran a Mage game blatantly based on Die Hard. I called it Wiz Hard. It was good fun. I need to work on my Alan Rickman impression, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:44:46-08:00","id":410383,"title":"","content":"I've never done this exactly.. in fact, a long time ago I abruptly ended a campaign because a new movie came out that we all went to see, and it basically exposed the core of my story before I had exposed it in game. I couldn't stand the fact that now I had it hanging over my head, and I didn't want to explain how &quot;I thought of it first!&quot;.<br /> <br /> That was when The Matrix came out, the original, in theaters - my story involved human brains being harvested and used as computer processing units, and I dropped it basically the moment we all walked out of the theater.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since then I have grown up a lot and realized that I was being petty. I still don't directly duplicate anything for my games, but I borrow HEAVILY from EVERYTHING.<br /> <br /> Consider that some of the classic stories of literature can be summed up into a quick synopsis, and then elaborated back out again into a whole new story. You can do this with stuff like Hamlet (or the overused Romeo and Juliet), or something more modern like Cape Fear. Strip the basic story of all the details and then apply it to all your details.<br /> <br /> I also tend to soak up stuff when running low on inspiration. Watch movies, read books, articles, blogs, look at images... sometimes it makes things fire off in your brain or links two seemingly unrelated ideas. The end result usually looks nothing like the inspiration that spawned it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have considered using a pre-existing setting and creating a custom set of mechanical rules and such, but honestly once I begin to start doing research and popping out idea sketches, I feel more constrained by the pre-existing stuff than I do set free by it. That's when I usually start fusing shit together and as I said above, the end result usually looks nothing like the inspiration.<br /> <br /> Highlander is one of those I have always wanted to create a sort of Mage-clone of. I've had stories that borrowed from it a lot, but never really took the whole setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391478-have-you-ever-adapted-a-preexisting-story-for-a-game?p=391771#post391771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in terms of OWoD this past summer I played, and helped create, a Dark Ages: Werewolf game set in the world of A Song of Ice and Fire/Game of Thrones, albeit around ten years before Robert's Rebellion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like fun. I would play in such a thing, and enjoy every minute of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited"